creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:41.8466111Z Note: a multi-user installation is possible. See https://nix.dev/manual/nix/stable/installation/installing-binary.html#multi-user-installation
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:41.8474309Z ^[[1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer^[[0m
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:41.8560503Z ^[[32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:41.8569768Z ^[[0m
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:41.8570385Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:41.8571074Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:41.8571367Z 
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:41.8571896Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:41.8572288Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:41.8572530Z 
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:41.8572714Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:41.8573042Z    if you are ready to continue.
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:41.8573201Z 
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:41.8573570Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [30001..30008])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 30000)^[[0m
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:41.8574365Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:41.8574973Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:41.8575447Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:41.8575702Z 
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:41.8575957Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:41.8576305Z 
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:41.8576622Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:41.8577325Z    can use Nix.
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:41.8577574Z 
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:41.8577728Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:41.8577872Z 
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:41.8578164Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:41.8578550Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:41.8584810Z 
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:41.8584955Z I will:
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:41.8585230Z 
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:41.8585510Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:41.8585957Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:41.8586325Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:41.8586664Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:41.8586911Z  - install Nix in /nix
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:41.8587180Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:41.8587525Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:41.8587890Z    /root
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:41.8597799Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:41.8598352Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:41.8607755Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:41.8608195Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:41.8608517Z 
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:41.8609629Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mReady to continue?
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:41.8610080Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:41.8625458Z 
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:41.8625950Z ^[[34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:41.8634981Z ^[[0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:41.8635401Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:41.8635926Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:41.8636186Z 
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:41.8636415Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:41.8636712Z 
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:41.8636993Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:41.8637571Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:41.8637892Z 
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:41.8638050Z If you would like to
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:41.8638534Z see the output, try like this:
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:41.8638861Z 
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:41.8639089Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:41.8639428Z   $ sh ./install-nix
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:41.8639562Z 
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:41.8639568Z 
creation	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:41.8639778Z ^[[32m~~> Checking for artifacts of previous installs
