fast	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:43.2659649Z Note: a multi-user installation is possible. See https://nix.dev/manual/nix/stable/installation/installing-binary.html#multi-user-installation
fast	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:43.2667908Z ^[[1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer^[[0m
fast	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:43.2763573Z ^[[32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
fast	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:43.2772622Z ^[[0m
fast	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:43.2773239Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
fast	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:43.2773911Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
fast	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:43.2774295Z 
fast	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:43.2774978Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
fast	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:43.2775708Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
fast	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:43.2776150Z 
fast	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:43.2776422Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
fast	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:43.2776766Z    if you are ready to continue.
fast	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:43.2776929Z 
fast	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:43.2777301Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [30001..30008])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 30000)^[[0m
fast	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:43.2777794Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
fast	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:43.2778192Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
fast	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:43.2778801Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
fast	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:43.2778961Z 
fast	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:43.2779124Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
fast	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:43.2779350Z 
fast	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:43.2779533Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
fast	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:43.2779865Z    can use Nix.
fast	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:43.2779982Z 
fast	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:43.2780093Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
fast	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:43.2780253Z 
fast	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:43.2780622Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
fast	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:43.2781035Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
fast	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:43.2783125Z 
fast	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:43.2783270Z I will:
fast	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:43.2783526Z 
fast	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:43.2783727Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
fast	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:43.2784079Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
fast	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:43.2784447Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
fast	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:43.2784928Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
fast	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:43.2785182Z  - install Nix in /nix
fast	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:43.2785420Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
fast	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:43.2785780Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
fast	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:43.2786144Z    /root
fast	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:43.2796071Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
fast	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:43.2797039Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
fast	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:43.2804926Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
fast	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:43.2805687Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
fast	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:43.2805981Z 
fast	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:43.2806445Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mReady to continue?
fast	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:43.2806973Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
fast	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:43.2820774Z 
fast	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:43.2821618Z ^[[34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
fast	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:43.2829962Z ^[[0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
fast	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:43.2830805Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
fast	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:43.2831455Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
fast	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:43.2831771Z 
fast	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:43.2832013Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
fast	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:43.2832363Z 
fast	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:43.2832659Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
fast	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:43.2833243Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
fast	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:43.2833623Z 
fast	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:43.2833786Z If you would like to
fast	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:43.2834174Z see the output, try like this:
fast	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:43.2834398Z 
fast	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:43.2834581Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
fast	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:43.2834908Z   $ sh ./install-nix
fast	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:43.2835045Z 
fast	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-10-22T15:08:43.2835053Z 
